<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFrameworks>net48;net452;netstandard2.0;netstandard2.1</TargetFrameworks>
		<SignAssembly>true</SignAssembly>
		<Authors>Trixxit</Authors>
		<Version>2.0.45</Version>
		<Description>Bwaaaa.</Description>
		<NodeReuse>false</NodeReuse>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<PackageTags>Debugging;RemoveBoilerplate;ILWeaving;Fody;Cecil;AOP</PackageTags>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>
			- ATTRIBUTE MAJOR!
			- Configuration is setup, or at least mostly.
			- All non-packing logic has been moved out of TrixxInjection and into TrixxInjection.Framework.
			- This is a DEBUG build to test if the Creation and Deletion attributes, as well as the Module type injection and StaticFileHandling works.
			- v2.0.1: (Immediete breakpointer is on).
			- v2.0.2: Fixed Assembly resolving, disabled immediete breakpoint.
			- 2.0.3: Fixed Assembly Expression tree mapping when methods had the same name.
			- ..4: Fixed incorrect default log path.
			- ..5: FrameworkMemory is now loaded in memory.
			- ..6: Undid ..5 change, moved framework copy logic from csproj to inside weaver execution.
			- ..7: Attempting to improve Framework stuff
			- ..8: Weave should now self support it's framework dll, and properly load it.
			- ..9: 'Cannot find netstandard.dll' issue - immediete breakpointing enabled
			- ..10: Decoupled Framework and Weaver, instead preferring to reference framework as an external package dependancy
			- ..11: Build
			- ..12: Changed LoadConfigurator from using a ValueTuple return to an out variable
			- ..13: Refactored configuration to use an assembly attribute in the framework instead of a class, changed logic to account for this.
			- ..14: Rebuild
			- ..16: Relocated markers namespace from TrixxInjection.Attributes to TrixxInjection.Framework.Attributes and Forgot to update Framework in prior versions
			- ..17: NuGet Fix?
			- ..18: Updated attribute scan name to match actual
			- ..19: Small change with attribute values
			- ..20: Removed Configurator class completely and updated logic for attribute
			- ..21: Fixed small issue where Config..Attribute was double named ( strong naming :c )
			- ..22: [RELEASE BUILD] Improve config parsing method to actually function as intended and removed forced breaker.
			- ..23: Back to debug build as things aren't working
			- ..24: Fixed type-method tree death
			- ..25: Disabled force debug breaking
			- ..26: Fixed Configure Injection to actually use the correct reference
			- ..27: Updated AddLog injection, time for an attribute test.
			- ..28: Updated Framework file handling.
			- ..29: Updated Namespace for Attribute handling.
			- ..30: Refactored Attribute Processing to use method infos instead of Delegates, as Fody doesnt like delegates
			- ..31: Added Developer Breaking for Attributes during processing. Use flags.
			- ..32: Forgot to update Framework in last build
			- ..33: Rebuild
			- ..34: Added autogenerated exposers for the otherwise private attribute methods, as without them NuGet removes them, being unused and all.
			- ..35: Added DEV__AttributesToBreakTo to attribute processor as I had forgotten it (no wonder it wasnt working)
			- ..36: rebuild
			- ..37: Added startup injection flag for breaking at Module class
			- ..38: Fixed the type misnaming.
			- ..39: Updated Framework references
			- ..40: Added a Return code to the module constructor... whoops
			- ..41: Added a pop, might need that yk
			- ..42: Resolved incorrect method path naming. ( I keep forgetting the .Framework :c )
			- ..43: Huge backend overall, now with a nice IL wrapper for easier writing. Needs to test to see if it all works now.
			- ..44: Added what could be a redundant return (redundant in some cases)
			- ..45: Corrected improper instruction sequence inversion.
		</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<PackageOutputPath>$(SolutionDir)..\nugets</PackageOutputPath>
		<RunPostBuildEvent>OnOutputUpdated</RunPostBuildEvent>
		<DebugType>portable</DebugType>
		<TargetsForTfmSpecificBuildOutput>$(TargetsForTfmSpecificBuildOutput)</TargetsForTfmSpecificBuildOutput>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="Fody" Version="6.6.4" PrivateAssets="none" />
		<PackageReference Include="FodyPackaging" Version="6.6.4" PrivateAssets="All" />
		<PackageReference Include="TrixxInjection.Framework" Version="1.0.8" IncludeAssets="All" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<Target Name="CopyLatestPackage" AfterTargets="Pack">
		<Exec Command="call &quot;$(SolutionDir)..\nugets\weaverCopy.bat&quot;" />
	</Target>
</Project>
